# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OWNER INPUT REQUIRED - the one remaining rights input for the 0.4 release (blocker B2).
# No name, affiliation, ORCID, date or identifier below has been invented. Fill all of the following in
# one pass, here and in the two pyproject.toml files, then delete this block:
#   1. authors:      replace each placeholder field of every entry, and add one entry per author in the
#                    agreed order. cff-version 1.2.0 requires at least one author, each with at least a
#                    name field; affiliation and orcid are optional.
#   2. pyproject.toml (root) authors - the same list, as name/email tables.
#   3. assistant/pyproject.toml - add the same authors list (it currently declares none).
#   4. date-released - add on the day of release (CFF expects YYYY-MM-DD).
#   5. the archive identifier - add a cff `doi` field only once one is actually minted.
# The MIT licence itself needs none of this: its copyright line, "The RNPLens authors", is the owner's
# explicit choice and is already carried verbatim by both distributions. What is missing is the citable
# authorship, not the grant.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use RNPLens, please cite the accompanying manuscript (in preparation) and this software release.
  PLACEHOLDERS: the author list, affiliations, ORCIDs, release date and DOI must be supplied by the owner before
  release. The author list and affiliations are those of the authoritative manuscript, supplied by the
  project owner; none of them has been inferred from git history.
title: "RNPLens: evaluation and diagnostic tools for protein-RNA complex predictions"
type: software
version: 0.4.0.dev0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JeanWen-Lab/RNPLens"
authors:
  - family-names: "Parker"
    given-names: "Brian J."
    affiliation: "Biological Data Science Institute, Australian National University, Canberra, Australia; ARC Centre of Excellence for the Mathematical Analysis of Cellular Systems, Canberra, Australia"
    email: "Brian.Parker@anu.edu.au"
  - family-names: "Wen"
    given-names: "Jiayu"
    affiliation: "John Curtin School of Medical Research, Australian National University, Canberra, Australia; The Shine-Dalgarno Centre for RNA Innovation, Australian National University, Canberra, Australia; ARC Centre of Excellence for the Mathematical Analysis of Cellular Systems, Canberra, Australia"
    email: "Jiayu.Wen@anu.edu.au"
abstract: >-
  RNPLens assesses existing protein-RNA complex predictions: reference-based structural accuracy on the DockQ route
  (Evaluate), reference-free descriptive agreement and contacts among predictions (Report, region, grouping, an
  offline Mol* viewer) and evidence-traced explanations and Methods records, through explicit commands or an optional
  AI-guided assistant (experimental). It does not predict structures and gives no calibrated probability of
  correctness. In 0.4, Evaluate's four-axis geometry route and the user-facing Diagnose workflow are blocked.
keywords:
  - protein-RNA complex
  - structure prediction
  - model evaluation
  - DockQ
  - structural biology
